
## Kit additions: requirement IDs

Add a `## Requirements` section to `TASK_BRIEF.md` right after `## Evaluation`, one testable
requirement per line with a stable ID and a priority (must, should or could):

```markdown
## Requirements
- REQ-001 (must): <one testable requirement>
- REQ-002 (should): <one testable requirement>
```

- Never reuse or renumber an ID; a dropped requirement keeps its number unused.
- Then run `kit req sync`: it records them in `.kit/work/trace.json` and raises the revision
  of every requirement whose line changed.
- Link each test with `kit trace link TC-001 --req REQ-001 --locator <file>::<test> --case
  normal|boundary|error|counterexample`. A must requirement needs one test that is not normal.
- Before declaring the task done run `kit trace check`; exit 1 lists untested, weak or stale
  requirements and tests that point to unknown ones.
